name air-tier-refused
timeout 60

# THE TIER GATE BITES — doc/modules/air/module.md §Spec 5's admission rule, and it is a ZUSICHERUNG
# rather than a comfort.
#
# doc/pilot.md's close-combat law INVERTS an identified roll plant (p_dot = -a*p + K*da). With another
# aircraft's plant it is not a limiter but an oscillator, and the two numbers are per-airframe
# MEASUREMENTS: the MiG-29 rolls 2.6x harder for the same stick than the F-16 (a = 0.819 / K = 201
# against 0.734 / 78.7). A GENERATED deck has no plant at all until step 7 of the flight-model recipe
# measures one on it — and step 8 grants the tier only once the deck has also passed the deviation bands
# of recipe §7.1.
#
# SINCE 2026-07-29 FOUR ROWS HAVE PASSED THEM and carry their measured plant (`f15c` 0.680712/176.220,
# `mig21` 0.724278/318.528, `mirf1` 0.745189/273.051, `f5e` 0.757465/322.722, all printed by
# `make -C sim test-air` as anchors ROLL-A / ROLL-K). SIX HAVE NOT, and `mig17` is one of them — 2 of
# its 7 judged anchors are outside their band, so step 8 has not run on it and its plant is still zero.
#
# `mig17` is a T2 row — a visual fighter, guns and eyes, the tier that OWNS `bfm` — and it is refused
# anyway, which is the point twice over: the gate reads the MEASUREMENT and not the tier label, and it
# keeps biting on exactly the rows whose decks have not earned the phase.
#
# READING RULE: exit 1 is the PASS. events.log must carry
#   ERROR module SET_INVALID_VALUE key=task value=bfm reason="this row's ROLL PLANT IS UNMEASURED ..."
#   ERROR mission SET_REJECTED key=task value=bfm
# and the run must never start. A run that FLIES is the failure — that is a catalogue cell flying the
# close-combat law on somebody else's aeroplane.

unit fresco
  team hostile
  module mig17
  spawn 46.90000 6.40000 4000 90.0 400
  set gear up
  set task bfm
  wp 46.90000 7.00000 4000 400
